{
  "id": "vacuum_pipes___pressure_loss_vs__air_flow",
  "title": "Vacuum Pipes - Pressure Loss vs. Air Flow",
  "description": "Calculate pressure drops in vacuum pipe lines. Based on initial vacuum pressure of 20 in Hg (67% vacuum) and steel pipes schedule 40.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Pressure Drop Calculation\n\nCalculate pressure drops in vacuum pipelines for steel pipes schedule 40.\n\n### Conversion Factors\n- 1 in Hg = 3.37 kPa\n- 1 scfm = 0.472 nl/s\n\n### Reference\nBased on initial vacuum pressure: **20 in Hg (67% vacuum)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "air_flow_scfm",
          "label": "Air Flow",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "scfm",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "pipe_diameter_inches",
          "label": "Pipe Diameter",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "inches",
          "defaultValue": 1
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "pressure_drop_in_hg_per_100ft",
          "label": "Pressure Drop (in Hg/100 ft)",
          "formula": "inputs.air_flow_scfm * 0.05",
          "unit": "in Hg/100 ft",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "air_flow_nl_s",
          "label": "Air Flow",
          "formula": "inputs.air_flow_scfm * 0.472",
          "unit": "nl/s",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_drop_kpa_per_100m",
          "label": "Pressure Drop (kPa/100 m)",
          "formula": "inputs.air_flow_scfm * 0.05 * 3.37",
          "unit": "kPa/100 m",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Pipe Diameter (in)",
        "Air Flow (scfm)",
        "Pressure Drop (in Hg/100 ft)",
        "Air Flow (nl/s)",
        "Pressure Drop (kPa/100 m)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          0.5,
          10,
          0.5,
          4.72,
          1.685
        ],
        [
          0.75,
          20,
          1,
          9.44,
          3.37
        ],
        [
